Ticket #4471 was merged as one issue: "dates parse mm/dd in eu locales." It is three.

## The three causes

**parser** (374 reports, 11 tenants): The shared date parser reads every date month-first
(MM/DD). Tenants whose locale writes the day first (DD/MM) get day and month swapped in
invites and reminders. Affects `app` and `email` channels.

**hint** (33 reports, 3 tenants): Booking form v3 shows `MM/DD/YYYY` as its date hint.
Users in day-first locales follow the hint and type month-first, but the form reads the
input in the tenant's locale (day-first). Day and month swap again — a different bug, only
on the `form` channel, only for tenants on booking-v3: alder.physio, copper.studio,
pale.harbour.

**off-by-one** (5 reports, 4 tenants): Bookings land on the adjacent day — one day off,
not a month/day swap. The desk read these as a one-day move (desk-notes `oneDayMove`).
Likely a timezone or date-boundary bug: R-41344 shows Lisbon and Toronto getting different
days for the same meeting.

<Callout kind="warn">
These need separate fixes. The parser fix does not help form users who followed the hint,
and neither fix addresses the off-by-one timezone issue.
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Why the desk missed it

The dedupe rule ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) merges on subject
alone. Reports about both bugs carry subjects like "Date is wrong" and "Month and day
swapped?" — the same words, different causes. The channel and the tenant's booking form
decide the cause, not the subject.

## What to do

File each cause as its own ticket. The parser bug is the larger one; the hint bug needs a
form-side fix (either change the hint to match the locale, or change the form to read what
the hint says). The off-by-one reports need a timezone investigation.

